    "body": "Fixes #41313.\n\nTag jump expanded every tag filename for environment variables before\nchecking it, so a literal dollar sign — decoded from a `file://` URI such\nas `file:///home/user/a.%24b.tsx`, or listed verbatim in a tags file —\nwas replaced with the empty string and the jump failed with `E429`.\nEscaping the name in `_tagfunc.lua` (#41398) was the wrong layer: the\nbackslash became literal and raw URIs no longer reached autocmd\nconsumers untouched, so it was reverted (#41489).\n\nThis instead fixes the consumption side in `expand_tag_fname()`: when\nexpansion changes the name but the result does not exist, the unexpanded\nname is kept. Jumps that already worked are unaffected — an expansion\nthat resolves to an existing path is used exactly as before — and\nproducer data (`item.fname`, URIs) stays verbatim, so raw `jdt://` URLs\nstill reach `BufReadCmd` consumers untouched.\n\n`%` needs no change on this path: it is not in `PATH_ALL_WILDCARDS`,\nso it never enters this expansion; `%24`-style escapes keep decoding\ncorrectly in `vim.uri_to_fname()`.\n\nRegression test drives a real `:tag` jump through a tagfunc returning a\n`$` filename with the variable set (fails with `E429` before the fix).\n\nNot verified locally: no build toolchain for Neovim in this environment,\nso compilation and the functional suite still need CI. The C change only\nadds a guarded fallback around the existing `ExpandOne` call.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-17T11:50:28Z",
